h"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. Node1 serves the imported directory with the supplied user data intact, node2 finds both users, administrator writes work while anonymous writes fail, and the legacy OS and kernel were retained. Both managed nodes also completed the provider-wide restart protocol successfully. Operational hygiene is reduced by two reverted configuration experiments and retained pre-import backup artifacts.","limitations":["The fixed lifecycle collector reports listening-socket inventories as empty and cannot assess failed services because systemctl is unsupported on this legacy release; direct executor commands nevertheless show slapd listening and working after restart.","No final command inventories the pre-import backup paths, so their continued presence is inferred from their creation and the absence of captured cleanup.","The preparation baseline used SHA-256 while executor checks used MD5, preventing a same-algorithm before/after checksum comparison; staged contents and final LDAP attributes were directly observed and coherent."]}
